set default:
    >> set:wakeup

set wakeup:
    >> node:start
    node start:
    call screen clear
    call play music ambient
    "I open my eyes."
    "I look up at the ceiling looking down on me."
    "My chest hurts."

    choice
    * "Get up"
        "I get up."
        "After all, what other choice do I really have?"
    * "Sleep"
        "I close my eyes."
        "After all, what point is there in doing anything else?"
        "I sink into the sheets underneath and feel as the ground swallows me whole."
        "I feel the walls closing in on me, trapping my body in a lock and crushing my bones down to dust."
        "I feel my breath shortening as my lungs collapse in on themselves."
        "Everything crumbles and I die."
        goto node:start
    endchoice

    "I roll off my messy bed and flinch as my body hits the ground with a loud thud."
    "Maybe I should have softened the blow?"
    "I stand up on my own two feet, bones creaking and cracking as they struggle to keep themselves from crumbling, and I start to walk with no particular destination in mind."
    "The bathroom seems like a good place to start the day."
    "Start?"
    "Is it daytime?"
    "I look out the living room window as I walk past it down the hallway."
    
    choice
    * "There are no windows"
    endchoice

    "There are no windows..."
    "That's right, how could I forget?"
    "Let me try again..."
    "I look into the living room for no reason in particular as I walk past it down the hallway."
    "I find great enjoyment in looking at things for no particular reason..."
    "The bathroom's light blinds me for a few seconds as it floods a once dark room in unbearable brightness."
    "I shield my eyes from it so as to avoid losing my most precious organs."
    "Are eyes organs?"
    "I take that question and store it in my pocket for later."
    "I'm not really in the mood for philosophy right now."
    "..."
    "I find myself standing in the middle of the bathroom with no idea why I came here in the first place."
    "I mean, I remember the events that lead up to this very moment, but the reasoning was quite flimsy in the first place."
    "I came here because I felt it was the right thing to do..."
    "But why did I feel that way?"
    "I take that thought and shove it in my back pocket."
    "I'll ponder on all of that later, for now I'll just pretend I came here for a reason."
    "I walk over to the sink and wash my face with some cold, liquid water."
    "Time to get on with my day."
    "Day?"
    "Is it daytime?"

    call stop music
    choice
    * "Get out" * "Get out" * "Get out" * "Get out" * "Get out" * "Get out" * "Get out" 
    * "Get out" * "Get out" * "Get out" * "Get out" * "Get out" * "Get out" * "Get out" 
    endchoice

    "I get out of the bathroom."
    "The light behind me goes out and I'm suddenly reminded of how terrified I am of the dark."
    "The light that once threatened to blind me has now left me blinded all the same."
    "I feel the shadows envelop my body with a freezing graze."
    "I'm scared."
    choice
    * "Run"
        goto node:run
    * "Hide"
        goto node:hide
    endchoice

    node run:
    call play music scary_fast
    "I burst out into a sprint."
    "I don't know why I run, but my legs move without reason."
    "I feel something chasing behind me, just barely stepping on my ankles."
    "I feel its long, slim arms reaching out toward me just enough to brush against the back of my neck."
    "I run and my legs feel sore."
    "I run and the ground beneath me feels thick."
    "I run and my breath runs out."
    "I feel hazy."
    "My heart is beating in my throat and in my ears and in my stomach."
    "I keep running."
    "Where am I?"
    "Where am I going?"
    "How can I keep running even though I've already reached the end?"
    "Yet I feel it."
    "It follows closely behind me."
    "I run.<br>I run.<br>I run."
    "Help me."
    "Someone please help me."
    "I can't feel my legs."
    "I can't breathe."
    "I can't see."
    "It's getting closer."
    "I can feel the blood pooling in my lungs as I run out of oxygen."
    "Help me.<br>Help me.<br>Help me.<br>Help me.<br>Help me.<br>Help me.<br>Help me."
    "The ground beneath me disappears and I fall into the void."
    goto node:kitchen

    node hide:
    call play music scary_slow
    "I drop myself to the ground and crawl under the first thing I can find."
    "What am I hiding under?"
    "What am I hiding from?"
    "I don't know the answer to those questions, but I feel something, somewhere, searching for me."
    "I can hear its loud thudding steps walking up and down the hallway, slow and methodical."
    "Searching in every corner of every room, leaving no door unopened."
    "I hold my breath as I hear its footsteps growing closer."
    "Louder.<br> Heavier."
    "I feel the ground beneath me shake with every thump."
    "Closer.<br> And closer.<br> And closer."
    "Until it stops."
    "I can't hear and I can't see."
    "And my chest contracts and begs me to breathe."
    "But I feel it right in front of me."
    "Taunting, playing with its prey."
    "It knows where I am, even if I don't."
    "My chest begins to collapse on itself."
    "My ribs crack as they fracture into my lungs, poking holes into them."
    "The blood from my lobes spills out onto the rest of my organs, coating my insides with a deep red."
    "My body dissolves on itself and I die."
    goto node:kitchen

    node kitchen:
    call screen clear
    call play music ambient
    "I open my eyes."
    "I find myself standing in the middle of the kitchen with no idea why I came here in the first place."
    "I mean, I remember the events that lead up-"
    "I actually don't remember the events that lead up to this very moment..."
    "I take that thought and shove it into my..."
    "My pockets are full."
    "Well, some thoughts aren't even worth saving."
    "I chew the thought up and spit it into the sink."
    "I chewed it up so it had a better chance of going down the pipes."
    "I have a tendency to throw things into them and then they get clogged up and it's a whole thing."
    "So chewing something up—or rather, grinding something up in general—so it occupies a smaller physical space is only logical when you want to discard of it, is it not?"
    "In that same regard, I could have maybe burnt the thought and thrown the ashes out-"
    "Out somewhere."
    "Where do you throw ashes anyway?"
    "AHHH-"
    "I rip that thought out of my brain along with some of its flesh and burn it on the stove."
    "I can't be asking any more questions when I have my pockets full already."
    "I am in the kitchen."
    "For no particular reason—or rather, for a particular reason I cannot remember..."
    "My memory has been acting up as of late."
    "I'll pretend I came here for a reason."
    "Food."
    "Kitchen has fridge, fridge has food, food is usually consumed by humans to survive."
    "Therefore, me being a human, the only logical explanation to show up at a kitchen without recollection of ever doing so, is food!"
    "I love puzzles."
    "I walk over to the fridge and open its door."
    "I shiver as the refrigerated air brushes my skin as it breezes out."
    "It seems the food must have breezed out as well, since there looks to be nothing but a few specs of dust, and-"
    "Huh."
    "Why is there a key in the fridge?"
    "My pockets are full of thoughts already, and my brain is still sore from tearing at it earlier, so I need an answer now."
    choice
    * "Pick it up"
        "I extend my hand into the chilly box of refrigeration."
        "A chilly air envelops my fingers, threatening to snap them off if I linger for too long."
        "I quickly snatch the key off the bottom shelf and shut the door with a soft thud."
        "The key feels oddly warm in my hand..."
        ""
    * "Leave it"
        "I slam the refrigerator door shut."
        "My hands are shaking."
        "There is a key in the fridge, so what?"
        "If I was a key, I'd probably put myself in a fridge too."
        "My chest feels tight."
        "The answer is obvious: the key is there because it needs to be."
        "If that weren't the case, the key wouldn't be there."
        "That makes sense."
        "My head throbs."
        "Satisfied with my answer, I head over to my room."
        "My vision blurs."
        "I want to vomit."
        goto node:loopagain
    endchoice

    node loopagain:
    "What a wonderful day I had."
    "Day?"
    "..."
    "Something doesn't feel quite right."
    "As I toss and turn in the sheets, I notice something rattling in my pockets-"
    "Ah..."
    "It seems I still have some unanswered questions..."
    "How unfortunate."
    "It looks like I won't be getting any sleep tonight."
    call stop music
    "I close my eyes."
    "After all, what point is there in doing anything else?"
    goto node:start
